{"id":"mahabharata-3-026","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":26,"title":"षड्विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 26 · Markandeya visits","summary":{"en":"The sage Markandeya visits the Pandavas and smiles at their hardship; he explains that he remembers Rama, who also lived in the forest at his father's command. He tells Yudhishthira that he will return to his kingdom after keeping his word.","kn":"ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯ ಮಹರ್ಷಿ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗಿ ಅವರ ಕಷ್ಟ ಕಂಡು ನಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ತಂದೆಯ ಆಜ್ಞೆಯಿಂದ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ವಾಸಿಸಿದ ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನನ್ನು ನೆನಪಿಸಿಕೊಂಡೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಮಾತು ಉಳಿಸಿಕೊಂಡ ಮೇಲೆ ರಾಜ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳುವೆ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"ऋषि मार्कण्डेय पाण्डवों से मिलने आते हैं और उनके कष्ट पर मुस्कराते हैं; वे बताते हैं कि उन्हें श्रीराम का स्मरण हुआ, जो पिता की आज्ञा से वन में रहे थे। वे युधिष्ठिर से कहते हैं कि वचन निभाकर वे अपने राज्य में लौटेंगे।","te":"మార్కండేయ మహర్షి పాండవులను సందర్శించి వారి కష్టాన్ని చూసి చిరునవ్వు నవ్వుతాడు; తండ్రి ఆజ్ఞతో అడవిలో నివసించిన శ్రీరాముడు గుర్తుకొచ్చాడంటాడు. మాట నిలబెట్టుకున్న తర్వాత రాజ్యానికి తిరిగి వెళ్తావని యుధిష్ఠిరునికి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"மார்க்கண்டேய முனிவர் பாண்டவர்களைச் சந்தித்து அவர்கள் துன்பத்தைக் கண்டு புன்னகைக்கிறார்; தந்தையின் ஆணையால் காட்டில் வாழ்ந்த ஸ்ரீராமர் நினைவுக்கு வந்தார் என்கிறார். வாக்கைக் காத்தபின் அரசுக்குத் திரும்புவாய் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரரிடம் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ പാണ്ഡവരെ സന്ദർശിച്ച് അവരുടെ ക്ലേശം കണ്ട് പുഞ്ചിരിക്കുന്നു; പിതാവിന്റെ കല്പനപ്രകാരം കാട്ടിൽ വസിച്ച രാമനെ താൻ ഓർക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. വാക്കു പാലിച്ചശേഷം യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ തന്റെ രാജ്യത്തേക്ക് മടങ്ങുമെന്ന് മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.26; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तत्काननं प्राप्य नरेन्द्रपुत्राः\nसुखोचिता वासमुपेत्य कृच्छ्रम् ।\nविजह्रुरिन्द्रप्रतिमाः शिवेषु\nसरस्वतीशालवनेषु तेषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching that forest, the princes, used to comfort and now enduring hardship, lived there and roamed like Indras through the pleasant sal woods along the Sarasvati."}},{"n":2,"text":"यतींश्च सर्वान्स मुनींश्च राजा\nतस्मिन्वने मूलफलैरुदग्रैः ।\nद्विजातिमुख्यानृषभः कुरूणां\nसंतर्पयामास महानुभावः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull of the Kurus, a man of great spirit, satisfied all the ascetics and sages and the foremost brahmins of that forest with abundant roots and fruits."}},{"n":3,"text":"इष्टीश्च पित्र्याणि तथाग्रियाणि\nमहावने वसतां पाण्डवानाम् ।\nपुरोहितः सर्वसमृद्धतेजा-\nश्चकार धौम्यः पितृवत्कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhaumya, the household priest, radiant with every prosperity, performed for the Pandavas living in the great forest the sacrifices, the rites for the ancestors and the first-fruit offerings, like a father to the Kurus."}},{"n":4,"text":"अपेत्य राष्ट्राद्वसतां तु तेषा-\nमृषिः पुराणोऽतिथिराजगाम ।\nतमाश्रमं तीव्रसमृद्धतेजा\nमार्कण्डेयः श्रीमतां पाण्डवानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they lived away from their kingdom, the ancient sage Markandeya, of fierce and abundant radiance, came as a guest to the hermitage of the glorious Pandavas."}},{"n":5,"text":"स सर्वविद्द्रौपदीं प्रेक्ष्य कृष्णां\nयुधिष्ठिरं भीमसेनार्जुनौ च ।\nसंस्मृत्य रामं मनसा महात्मा\nतपस्विमध्येऽस्मयतामितौजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All-knowing and great-souled, he looked at Draupadi, Yudhishthira, Bhima and Arjuna, remembered Rama in his mind, and smiled, of unmeasured might, amid the ascetics."}},{"n":6,"text":"तं धर्मराजो विमना इवाब्रवी-\nत्सर्वे ह्रिया सन्ति तपस्विनोऽमी ।\nभवानिदं किं स्मयतीव हृष्ट-\nस्तपस्विनां पश्यतां मामुदीक्ष्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of dharma, rather dejected, said to him: \"All these ascetics are ashamed for me. Why do you seem to smile, as if delighted, looking at me before the ascetics' eyes?\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"न तात हृष्यामि न च स्मयामि\nप्रहर्षजो मां भजते न दर्पः ।\nतवापदं त्वद्य समीक्ष्य रामं\nसत्यव्रतं दाशरथिं स्मरामि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dear son, I am not delighted and I do not mock you; no pride born of joy possesses me. Seeing your misfortune today, I remember Rama, son of Dasharatha, who kept his vow of truth.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"स चापि राजा सह लक्ष्मणेन\nवने निवासं पितुरेव शासनात् ।\nधन्वी चरन्पार्थ पुरा मयैव\nदृष्टो गिरेरृष्यमूकस्य सानौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That same king, Partha, wandering with his bow in the forest together with Lakshmana, because of his father's command alone, was seen by me long ago on the slope of Mount Rishyamukha.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"सहस्रनेत्रप्रतिमो महात्मा\nमयस्य जेत नमुचेश्च हन्ता ।\nपितुर्निदेशादनघः स्वधर्मं\nवने वासं दाशरथिश्चकार ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The great-souled son of Dasharatha, like the thousand-eyed Indra, conqueror of Maya's kind and slayer of Namuchi's kind, blameless, lived in the forest at his father's order, as his own duty.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"स चापि शक्रस्य समप्रभावो\nमहानुभावः समरेष्वजेयः ।\nविहाय भोगानचरद्वनेषु\nनेशे बलस्येति चरेदधर्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He too, equal in power to Shakra, of great spirit and unconquerable in battles, gave up all comforts and lived in the forests, thinking 'I am not master of my strength,' and so he followed dharma.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"नृपाश्च नाभागभगीरथादयो\nमहीमिमां सागरान्तां विजित्य ।\nसत्येन तेऽप्यजयंस्तात लोका-\nन्नेशे बलस्येति चरेदधर्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kings such as Nabhaga and Bhagiratha conquered this earth bounded by the oceans, and yet by truth they won the worlds, dear son; not being masters of their strength, they followed dharma.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"अलर्कमाहुर्नरवर्य सन्तं\nसत्यव्रतं काशिकरूषराजम् ।\nविहाय राष्ट्राणि वसूनि चैव\nनेशे बलस्येति चरेदधर्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They say that Alarka, the good and truthful king of Kashi and Karusha, gave up his kingdoms and his riches; not being master of his strength, he followed dharma.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"धात्रा विधिर्यो विहितः पुराण-\nस्तं पूजयन्तो नरवर्य सन्तः ।\nसप्तर्षयः पार्थ दिवि प्रभान्ति\nनेशे बलस्येति चरेदधर्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The ancient rule laid down by the creator is honored by the good, best of men; the seven sages shine in the sky, Partha, because, not being masters of their strength, they follow dharma.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"महाबलान्पर्वतकूटमात्रा-\nन्विषाणिनः पश्य गजान्नरेन्द्र ।\nस्थितान्निदेशे नरवर्य धातु-\nर्नेशे बलस्येति चरेदधर्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Look, king, at the mighty elephants with tusks, big as mountain peaks; they stand under the creator's command, best of men, not masters of their strength, and so they follow dharma.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"सर्वाणि भूतानि नरेन्द्र पश्य\nयथा यथावद्विहितं विधात्रा ।\nस्वयोनितस्तत्कुरुते प्रभावा-\nन्नेशे बलस्येति चरेदधर्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Look, king, at all beings, each made by the creator just as it is; each acts according to its own origin and nature, not being master of its strength, and so follows dharma.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"सत्येन धर्मेण यथार्हवृत्त्या\nह्रिया तथा सर्वभूतान्यतीत्य ।\nयशश्च तेजश्च तवापि दीप्तं\nविभावसोर्भास्करस्येव पार्थ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By truth, by dharma, by fitting conduct and by modesty you have surpassed all beings, and your glory and splendor blaze, Partha, like the sun, the lord of light.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"यथाप्रतिज्ञं च महानुभाव\nकृच्छ्रं वने वासमिमं निरुष्य ।\nततः श्रियं तेजसा स्वेन दीप्ता-\nमादास्यसे पार्थिव कौरवेभ्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great-souled one, when you have lived through this hard forest exile as you promised, then you will take back from the Kauravas your splendid fortune, shining with your own radiance, O king.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"तमेवमुक्त्वा वचनं महर्षि-\nस्तपस्विमध्ये सहितं सुहृद्भिः ।\nआमन्त्र्य धौम्यं सहितांश्च पार्थां-\nस्ततः प्रतस्थे दिशमुत्तरां सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus to him in the midst of the ascetics and his friends, the great sage took leave of Dhaumya and the Pandavas, and set off toward the northern direction."}}]}]}